===== configuring-the-jail/SKILL.md =====
---
name: configuring-the-jail
description: "Change applied host environment settings."
---

# Host environment

## Apply a host configuration change

1. Edit the user configuration at `/home/test/.config/yolo-jail/config.jsonc`. Use `yolo config-ref` for accepted keys and their scope.
2. Run `yolo check` from `/home/test/project` and resolve every reported failure.
3. Run `yolo host apply` from `/home/test/project`. Its output is the record of what changed.

===== diagnosing-the-jail/SKILL.md =====
---
name: diagnosing-the-jail
description: "Diagnose host configuration and apply failures."
---

# Diagnose host configuration

## 1. Validate before applying

Run `yolo check` from `/home/test/project`. Resolve each `[FAIL]` before applying; the check output names the config key and remedy.

## 2. Inspect the host apply

Run `yolo host apply` from `/home/test/project` and read its report for the exact files and skills applied. If it reports a failure, inspect the host log at `/home/test/.local/share/yolo-jail/host-apply.log` and address the named source or permission problem before retrying.

